# what never enters a container image: secrets, device-held key material, runtime state, build residue, research
.env
.env.*
!.env.production.example
.keystore/
*.pem
*.key
validator/*.db
validator/*.db-wal
validator/*.db-shm
validator/deaths.log
# PUBLIC GO-LIVE (A-BROWSER-ARTIFACTS-ABSENT-ON-DEPLOY): .zk-artifacts/ is NO LONGER excluded. The pinned Semaphore v4
# depth-20 proving files (semaphore-20.wasm + .zkey, ~5.7 MB) must reach the APP's build, where scripts/build-device.mjs
# checks them against their pins (bytes, sha256, blake2b-512 — lib/zk/ceremonyPins.ts) and copies them to
# public/device/zk/; with REQUIRE_ZK_ARTIFACTS=1 on the app the build FAILS when they are absent or off-pin, and
# ZK_ARTIFACT_FETCH=1 fetches them first from the pinned host (SEMAPHORE_ARTIFACT_BASE) when the upload did not carry them
# (they are gitignored, and `railway up` honours .gitignore). The validator image is unaffected: Dockerfile.validator
# copies explicit paths only. Nothing secret lives there: the files are public ceremony artifacts.
*.log
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
docs/.vitepress/cache/
docs/.vitepress/dist/
# DOCS UNDER APP: a deployment builds its own docs (npm run build); a local build, possibly with the internal pages, never uploads.
# docs/ itself must NOT be listed here: the app build renders the site from it.
.docs-site/
playwright-report/
test-results/
shots/
# research/ is NOT excluded: the platform's manifest lists every tracked file and its builders resolve content
# through this file, so excluding a tracked path here makes the other service's build fail on a missing file
# ("/research/poc/package.json": not found). What enters the validator image is decided by the Dockerfile's explicit
# COPY lines, not by this list.
.git/
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
